From d456805d32b87b3be136ee4f3ece5aa1a4b2a500 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yaseen <20190myaseen@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 11:05:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Back office discoverability: first-run card in the Finance
 tab + a block in the carrier email
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Production check found the whole back office — payroll, expenses, IFTA, service log, accounting
export and two-way QuickBooks sync — had never been used once by any carrier, while every part of
it works (qbo_config is set on prod, both edge functions are ACTIVE, the redirect allowlist passes,
all write RPCs are granted). Nothing to debug; carriers simply do not know it is there.

- app/carrier/app.js: a first-run card at the top of Finance naming the four things and jumping to
  the right section. Shows only while the carrier genuinely has nothing (no QBO connection, no
  payroll entries, no expenses) and can be dismissed for good — anyone already keeping books never
  sees it. Jumps drive the same sec/paint() state the section nav drives.
- docs/CARRIER-EMAIL-DAILY-AVAILABILITY.md/.html: a 'while you're in there' block after the main
  availability message, so the email that is going out anyway carries the introduction. Table
  structure verified balanced and rendered.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NLBisLFyx9zVgJDMVRxc9M
---
